NickelOS: ChromeOS's own cursors for X11 apps. Wayland apps ask Exo for
cursor shapes by name (cursor-shape-v1, Chrome 0034) and get ChromeOS's
cursors; Xwayland sends images drawn from the X cursor theme at its own
size, so the cursor changed size and look over an X11 window (Steam).
Sommelier is also the X11 window manager: it now selects XFixes cursor
notifications on the root, which carry the current X cursor's name
(libXcursor names the theme cursors it loads: left_ptr, pointer, xterm,
...). A name with a cursor-shape-v1 shape (CSS names and X11's classic
ones, as other compositors map them) is shown as ChromeOS's own shape
(wp_cursor_shape_device_v1.set_shape); a cursor without one (an app's own
image, a hidden cursor) passes through as Xwayland's image, as before.
The image and the name arrive on different connections in either order,
so the last image is kept and shown again when the name has no shape.

